<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Ida (Crete)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Psiloritis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Ida, also called Psiloritis, is the highest mountain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, rising to 2,456 metres in the centre of the island. In Greek myth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> was raised in a cave on its slopes, and the Idaean Cave was a major sanctuary from the Minoan period into Roman times. Ancient cities such as Eleutherna and Axos lay on its foothills.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-ida-crete.jpg" alt="Mount Ida (Crete)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jerzy Strzelecki · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Psiloritis3(js).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
